    "episode_id": "case-cb4848dd6210-0004",
    "evidence": "Challenge to the claim 'Employee 4471 worked 42 hours this week.'\n\nThe only record of employee 4471's hours in this episode is the weekly timesheet, which lists five days:\n- Monday: 8\n- Tuesday: 8\n- Wednesday: 9\n- Thursday: 7\n- Friday: 8\n\nSum of the recorded hours: 8 + 8 + 9 + 7 + 8 = 40.\n\nThe claim asserts 42 hours. The recorded total is 40, which is 2 hours less than the claimed figure (42 - 40 = 2).\n\nThe timesheet record also states: 'No weekend shifts or overtime entries were recorded for this week.' That clause matters, because weekend shifts and overtime are the ordinary ways a weekly total could exceed the sum of five weekday figures. The record affirmatively excludes them, so there is no entry in evidence that could raise the total from 40 to 42. The five listed days are the complete set of days on the timesheet, with no duplicated or missing weekday rows.\n\nOn the record before the jury, the highest weekly total the evidence will support is 40 hours, and the claimed 42 hours is not supported by, and is contradicted by, the only hours record in the episode.\n\nI acknowledge the limit of this evidence: it establishes that the timesheet records 40 hours and that the record excludes weekend and overtime entries, not that 40 hours is necessarily the true number of hours the employee actually worked in the world. If some off-record source showed additional hours, the comparison would need redoing. Nothing in this episode supplies such a source, and the claim as posted is not supported by the record it rests on.",
    "evidence_hash": "0xca4d33234e3dfdeb415d8240b8213613da5a2dd08a6361f3a282bb863d9e281d",
