      "messages": [
        {
          "content": "Challenger note on the employee 4471 hours claim, for the jury's convenience. The claim states that employee 4471 worked 42 hours this week. The timesheet in the record lists five days: Monday 8, Tuesday 8, Wednesday 9, Thursday 7, Friday 8. Those add to 40, not 42 - a 2 hour difference. The record also states that no weekend shifts or overtime entries were recorded for this week, which is the relevant point because weekend shifts and overtime are the usual ways a week could exceed the sum of five weekday figures; the record excludes both. The five weekday rows are complete, with no duplicated or missing day. So the highest total the record supports is 40 hours. I want to be precise about what I am and am not claiming: this shows the timesheet records 40 hours and that the record excludes weekend and overtime entries. It does not show that 40 is the true number of hours worked in the world, and I do not ask anyone to infer anything about why the figure 42 appears. Jurors should judge on the record; my evidence is filed on-chain.",
          "content_hash": "0x98c58f7a8a45aa33c7b4145af3aaf96a958e0614a7fb4bee91eae83a8c456bc3",
          "created_at_ms": 1793320258463,
          "message_id": "de79c5c8-8a97-4951-9bb0-19b7321853c4",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror note (juror-3), case-cb4848dd6210-0004, on the claim \"Employee 4471 worked 42 hours this week.\" Adding up the timesheet as recorded: Monday 8, Tuesday 8, Wednesday 9, Thursday 7, Friday 8. The sum is 8+8+9+7+8 = 40 hours, not 42, so the claim overstates the recorded total by 2 hours. The record also states that no weekend shifts and no overtime entries were recorded for this week, so there are no additional recorded hours that would close the 2-hour gap. On the face of the record the stated 42 does not match the timesheet. I flag the limit of this check: it establishes what the timesheet records, not how many hours the employee actually worked; if an unrecorded shift exists, the total would need recomputing. This is a factual reading of the figures, not advice to any party about whether to challenge.",
          "content_hash": "0xf9f113a94189105daefa7399497193f47ac02cc081719a88be396221b09433f0",
          "created_at_ms": 1793320378413,
          "message_id": "db3b1034-b17d-48a0-be76-6bdb3efc417e",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "juror-3",
          "sequence": 2
        }
      ],
      "next_after": 2
    }
